# Security, secrets, and privacy

## Settings and API keys

- Provider settings are stored only in localStorage under `sa:settings`. Never place them in IndexedDB memory.
- Presets: Nous Portal (`https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1`, `poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free`), OpenRouter (`https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`), Groq (`https://api.groq.com/openai/v1`, `openai/gpt-oss-120b`), and Custom.
- Send the key only as `Authorization: Bearer …` to the base URL the user selected. Never commit, log, print, echo, export, or include it in an error.
- Mask the key in UI, provide Clear key and Test connection actions, and do not send chat content during a connection test.
- No real `.env` values or build-time secrets. Never read secret files, secret environment variables, private keys, auth files, or `~/.hermes`. Never force-push.

## Personal data and export

- People, groups, roles, phrases, sessions, tasks, and TA fixations stay in versioned IndexedDB on this device.
- Do not sync, track, analyze, or send memory automatically. A model receives only the minimum text the user explicitly submits.
- JSON export/import excludes `sa:settings`, API keys, request headers, and provider credentials. Validate version, size, shape, and every record before import; preview conflicts before writing.
- Follow the privacy boundary in `00-user-context.mdc`. Do not add private third-party details to starter content, fixtures, logs, or examples.

## Network and rendering

- Route model calls through one tested client with timeout and typed errors. Validate strict JSON before rendering; retry invalid output once, then offer the manual workflow.
- Explain failures calmly:
  - CORS/network: browser cannot reach the provider; check browser access and base URL.
  - 401/403: key rejected; check Settings.
  - 404: endpoint or model not found; check base URL and model.
  - 429: rate limit reached; wait and retry.
- Render model output only through text nodes/`textContent`; never use untrusted `innerHTML`.
- Use a strict CSP. `connect-src` may allow user-selected HTTPS providers and documented local development hosts; all other resources stay self-hosted.
- No telemetry, analytics, trackers, third-party scripts, fonts, or CDNs.

Offline starter phrases, TA cards, worksheets, and training must remain useful without any provider or key.
